From: Tomasz Figa <tomasz.figa@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] net: dsa: qca8k: fix bitmask calculation in QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL_LPI_EN

The QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL register (0x0100) controls MAC-side Low Power Idle
(LPI) on ports 1 through 5. The bits are allocated as pairs per port, with
LPI enable located at bit ((port + 1) * 2) (e.g. bit 12 for port 5).

However, the QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL_LPI_EN(_i) macro calculated this shift as
a raw integer without wrapping it in BIT(). Consequently, for port 5, the
macro evaluated to integer 12 (0x000c) instead of BIT(12) (0x1000). When
qca8k_set_mac_eee() updated the register, it manipulated unrelated low bits
(bits 3:2) instead of toggling the port's LPI enable bit.

Wrap the expression in BIT() so that the correct register bit is targeted.

Fixes: 6b93fb664fb2 ("net-next: dsa: add new driver for QCA8K")
Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa <tomasz.figa@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k.h
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k.h
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@
 
 /* EEE control registers */
 #define QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL				0x100
-#define  QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL_LPI_EN(_i)			((_i + 1) * 2)
+#define  QCA8K_REG_EEE_CTRL_LPI_EN(_i)			BIT((_i + 1) * 2)
 
 /* TRUNK_HASH_EN registers */
 #define QCA8K_TRUNK_HASH_EN_CTRL			0x270
